I have a somewhat successful monk going for the first time (I actually
got to level 14, not that I'm ready to take on Master Kaen yet,
though), and I have noticed several strange things:

1)  The intrinsics gained from increasing levels are not the same you
gain by eating corpses.  For instance, when I hit level 11, "You feel
cool".  Not much later, I ate a gelatinous cube corpse and had a
momentary chill.  What happens if a gremlin attacks and steals my fire
resistance?  Do I still have it from being at least level 11?  It's
all very confusing trying to keep track of resistances coming from so
many sources.

2)  Does it strike anyone else as totally useless that a monk, upon
crowning, receives a spellbook of restore ability?  I mean, by then,
you almost always will have a unicorn horn, which works quite well to
restore abilities.  Being crowned should give monks something much
more useful (as with wizards, assuming they don't already have it). 
Now, given that I've not played monks much, I'm not sure what that
would be.  Maybe a new artifact robe?  I don't have a good idea, but
it needs to be better than a completely useless spellbook... well, ok,
there is one use... exercising the appropriate spellcasting skill.

3)  Why do monks receive artifact weapons when sacrificing at altars? 
Maybe the code should check to see if the monk is adhering to "Never
hit with wielded weapon" conduct.  If so, give them a random spellbook
instead of a weapon.  My monk is trying to play weaponless (and
vegan), so artifact weapons aren't much use.  Spellbooks of
attack/enchantment/divination spells would be much more useful! 
Demonbane, on the other hand, is almost totally useless.  Maybe I
should see how much I can sell it for...

4)  This one is getting somewhat fanciful, but how about a new ability
for monks of high enough level:  enlightenment.  I mean, isn't
attaining enlightenment what being a monk is all about.  Maybe at a
certain level, monks would be able to #meditate.  This would take
several turns (similar to #pray, without the immunity to monster
attacks).  If undisturbed and the monk is successful (make a check
against some function of XL and WIS), they get the effects of an
uncursed potion of enlightenment.

